Location: Germany (remote)


Position Overview

As a Senior Backend Engineer, you will be part of a cross-functional and agile team of 5-7 people;
 Participate in the entire life cycle of the application;
 Work on a microservices based architecture using cutting edge technologies/libraries;
Work with front-end developers to integrate user-facing elements with server-side logic;
 Write clean and high-quality code, build prototypes, solve problems, profile and manage bottlenecks;
 Develop automated tests to ensure business requirements are met and enable regression testing.


Preferred experience

Experience in object-oriented software design and development of distributed infrastructure systems;
Using one or more server-side programming languages, preferably Ruby, Go, Python, Java, etc.;
 Experience with relational (e.g. MySQL, PostgreSQL) and non-relational (e.g. MongoDB, DynamoDB) databases;
 Experience with message brokers (e.g. RabbitMQ, Kafka, SQS);
 Solid fundamentals of computer science, algorithms and data structures;
 Analytical thinking and problem-solving skills;
 Excellent communication skills; written and spoken;
 Experience working as part of an agile software development team;
 Experience defining solutions and designing containerized applications (Kubernetes) in clouds (eg AWS, GCP) and microservices architectures.

Our company, Group 8 Security Solutions Inc (DBA Machine Learning Intelligence), is a financial technology and capital markets research firm that offers computational finance engineering services to retail and institutional investors. We provide quantitative strategies, risk models, and research tools with advanced functionality to help traders and investors make better decisions across all markets. Our goal is to empower private investors to diversify their portfolios and follow markets accurately. We also aim to support the capital markets towards better performance through regulation and transparency.

We are currently seeking a Business Development Manager (Performance Based) with knowledge of International capital markets. The ideal candidate is an expert in selling and representing software-based solutions, specifically SaaS web-based solutions for our clients. Our platform allows global users to keep track of critical market data relevant to retail and institutional investors, traders, academics, and quantitative developers.

The compensation for this role is performance-based, with a minimum salary range of $3000-$36000 USD per month, depending on the number of monthly or yearly clients acquired and recurring revenues. The agreement type is Independent Contractor, with a flexible work schedule and remote work location. The responsibilities include engaging with global clients, presenting the platform, collecting information, and instructing prospects on how to subscribe to the company's services. The candidate must have a minimum of a university or college graduation, with a preference for a Masters or PhD degree. They must also have advanced knowledge of international financial markets and be highly organized. Additional assets include certifications, brokerage accounts, and previous experience in investment management, data science, quantitative investing, and regulatory entities.

Please read our full job description attached;
This role is a good fit for a manger that has assisted other similar startups in the past, with good knowledge and capabilities in acquiring clients from a variety of international markets as well as advanced payment systems; advanced knowledge of SEO, web traffic, social media networks and automation would also be useful;

