You are responsible for the development of mechanical parts and assemblies for action video cameras;
You will work on translating product requirements into mechanical parts in a multidisciplinary and cross-site team.
 You analyse requirements and ensure that they are implemented;
Safeguarding functionality, performance, quality, reliability and manufacturability of products;

Thank you for your interest!

Please provide us with your:

a)	Cover letter;
b)	Complete CV and video portfolio. 

Incomplete submissions and requests that are not deemed to be genuine will not be processed. All our Concept Art is copyright protected and the selected applicants will have to sign an NDA (Non Disclosure Agreement) and a copy of a proof of identity.

PRO-PRODUCTION TASKS - 3D/CGI/VFX – 6 months: 

-	TOP PRIORITY: Unreal Engine 5.X (including conversion 4.X to 5.X) 3D ENVIRONMENTS - Six (6) SET/SCENES 3D Environments according to our Concept Art and Studies for UE suitable for 4K use with RED CAMERA files 4K RAW (REDCODE R3D) Aspect ratio: CinemaScope (2.39:1) / 4096x1716 which will be published as Digital Cinema Package ready for Printed format D-Cinema.  

- Polish/Improve SET/SCENES 3D Environments already built around 90%. (Including Six (6) Environments)

-	Workflow and compulsory deadlines : 
6 months including conversion and verification and adjustments of existent environments + 3 months of Post-production assistance.

-	Pipeline :
a)	Production: Upload all Concept Art / Studies review;
b)	Freelancer: Review the elements and start to prepare the requested environments;
Freelancer: Prepare the environments and submit weekly reports (one per week minimum) with multi-angle and multi camera position screenshots showing the progress of the work. During this process the freelancer will have an open line me so that our graphic department / Senior CGI consultant and film director could respond to further clarification or information that  might arise – The freelancer will have to prepare the 3D assets proposing high quality textures with variants or assist to find the appropriate texture and texturize/adjust the elements the production would require. Naturally, in the event we will need to buy assets, we will evaluate the purchase and validated according to the freelancer’s expertise and our budget possibilities. All purchases must be validated by written and we will place the orders and then send the assets to the freelancer. Normally, some assets will have to be slightly altered, please let us know if you have modelling knowledge to make some modifications. 
c)	Production: in +- 48hs the production will send back to the freelancer a review of her/his report with images and/or explanations until the SET/SCENE will receive a final validation – there will be no limited number of adjustments i.e. the freelancer will have to perform all required adjustments sharing her/his point of view on how to optimize the aimed results and respect the deadlines;
d)	All Production Assets must be delivered directly and exclusively to our DropBox account and on a Hard Drive provided by us  – including all native/matrices set of files and projects related to the 3D final assets – ready to use on any 3D Pro computer configuration. 
 

DELIVERABLES (Post-production):
- Video 360 of 4 circle degrees – 9 different camera positions: 0°/360° Full Resolution and Full Frame images with aspect ratio 4K Scope (2.39:1) – (best 4K quality allowed in Unreal Engine : frame size: 4096x1716;
- Video traveling - Horizontal and vertical traveling – to be determined according to the 360° results;
- 360 Panos TIFF files with lens distortion correction - frame size: 4096x1716 (16bit) and 8K Scope 8K = 8192 x 4320 (16-bit); 
- 9 camera placements (3 multiple files with 360 Panos) of SETS/SCENES: 1) Three at the centre (left / right / middle) - 2) Three at the one edge of the SET/SCENE (left / right / middle) - 2) Three at the other one edge of the SET/SCENE (left / right / middle) OBS: the edges of the rooms are delimited naturally – we will indicate the position for the exteriors in due course;
- ScreenShots (multiple files per set) We will send the camera position and angle instructions for each ScreenShot.

Best regards,

Mark Scott

